y.", "watch": "Fresh polling or a late shift in the national environment toward Republicans could tighten this into tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chris Pappas (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Hampshire's 1st District is an open seat after Chris Pappas left the race to run for Senate, removing a proven incumbent from the ballot. The district leans Democratic by about two points, and the 2026 national environment adds to that advantage. Stefany Shaheen benefits from roughly $2.2 million in outside support, while Anthony DiLorenzo has strong individual fundraising of about $5.1 million. National figures from both parties have campaigned in the district, and Republicans treat it as a pickup opportunity.\n\nThe only public poll, from the University of New Hampshire in late September, showed Shaheen ahead 46 to 42 among likely voters. Expert ratings cluster at Likely Democratic, and prediction markets put Democratic odds near 95 percent. The forecast expects Shaheen to win by a moderate margin, with the open-seat dynamic and thin polling keeping uncertainty elevated.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.937, "margin": 10.01}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9238, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9245, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8928, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8695, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.844, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.871, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8487, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8802, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8452, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8807, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8831, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8873, "margin": 7.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8466, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-0